{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-arc-space","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:arc-space","kind":"definition","title":"Arc space $\\mathcal{L}(X)$ of the brane tower","cites":["references/denef-loeser2001"],"tags":["arc-space","jet-scheme","brane-tower","motivic"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.ArcSpace","text":"arc-space.md","leanSource":"arc-space.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:arc-space\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> be a variety in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code>. Its <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>-th jet scheme</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}_n(X)</code> is the scheme representing the functor</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  R \\longmapsto \\mathrm{Hom}_{\\mathrm{Sch}}\\!\\bigl(\\mathrm{Spec}\\,R[t]/(t^{n+1}),\\; X\\bigr).</code></pre>\n<p>The <strong>arc space</strong> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> is the formal inverse limit</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{L}(X) = \\varprojlim_{n} \\mathcal{L}_n(X).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/arc-space.md","heading":"Definition","number":"6.1.10","page":"b/def-arc-space","qa":{"counts":{"pass":83,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":8,"unknown":0,"stale":64},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.LiftingDescentRoot.ArcSpace","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/arc-space.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
